tartCommand`"},"2719":{"id":"/project-conventions-812","page_id":"/project-conventions","tags":["conventions","contributing","safety","bazel","style"],"type":"text","url":"/project-conventions#documented-direct-invocations","content":"`bash .devcontainer/doctor.sh --quiet`"},"2720":{"id":"/project-conventions-813","page_id":"/project-conventions","tags":["conventions","contributing","safety","bazel","style"],"type":"text","url":"/project-conventions#documented-direct-invocations","content":"The doctor is the bootstrap that proves `bazelisk` is installed, so it cannot depend on `bazelisk`. Everywhere else uses `bazelisk run //:doctor`."},"2721":{"id":"/project-conventions-814","page_id":"/project-conventions","tags":["conventions","contributing","safety","bazel","style"],"type":"text","url":"/project-conventions#documented-direct-invocations","content":"CI `Install docs site dependencies`"},"2722":{"id":"/project-conventions-815","page_id":"/project-conventions","tags":["conventions","contributing","safety","bazel","style"],"type":"text","url":"/project-conventions#documented-direct-invocations","content":"`pip install -r docs/requirements.txt`, `npm ci`, `npx playwright install`"},"2723":{"id":"/project-conventions-816","page_id":"/project-conventions","tags":["conventions","contributing","safety","bazel","style"],"type":"text","url":"/project-conventions#documented-direct-invocations","content":"Provisions host tools and warms the npm/playwright caches that the later Bazel targets consume; no target installs a browser binary."},"2724":{"id":"/project-conventions-817","page_id":"/project-conventions","tags":["conventions","contributing","safety","bazel","style"],"type":"text","url":"/project-conventions#documented-direct-invocations","content":"CI `Validate gate (path-filter consistency)`"},"2725":{"id":"/project-conventions-818","page_id":"/project-conventions","tags":["conventions","contributing","safety","bazel","style"],"type":"text","url":"/project-conventions#documented-direct-invocations","content":"`bash scripts/ci_check_only.sh`"},"2726":{"id":"/project-conventions-819","page_id":"/project-conventions","tags":["conventions","contributing","safety","bazel","style"],"type":"text","url":"/project-conventions#documented-direct-invocations","content":"Deliberately Bazel-free so the gate needs no Bazel server or disk-cache cold start."},"2727":{"id":"/project-conventions-820","page_id":"/project-conventions","tags":["conventions","contributing","safety","bazel","style"],"type":"text","url":"/project-conventions#documented-direct-invocations","content":"`Makefile` fallback branches"},"2728":{"id":"/project-conventions-821","page_id":"/project-conventions","tags":["conventions","contributing","safety","bazel","style"],"type":"text","url":"/project-conventions#documented-direct-invocations","content":"`shellcheck`, `bats tests/bats/`, `cd dashboard && npm test`, `./fix.sh`"},"2729":{"id":"/project-conventions-822","page_id":"/project-conventions","tags":["conventions","contributing","safety","bazel","style"],"type":"text","url":"/project-conventions#documented-direct-invocations","content":"Reachable only when `bazelisk` is absent, which is the shim's stated purpose."},"2730":{"id":"/project-conventions-823","page_id":"/project-conventions","tags":["conventions","contributing","safety","bazel","style"],"type":"text","url":"/project-conventions#documented-direct-invocations","content":"A new exception needs a row here plus a comment at the call site saying why."},"2731":{"id":"/project-conventions-824","page_id":"/project-conventions","tags":["conventions","contributing","safety","bazel","style"],"type":"text","url":"/project-conventions#writing-it-bazel-first","content":"Every tracked file must be owned by a Bazel rule: a `srcs`/`data`/`tools`\nentry, an `exports_files` entry, a module-level list, a declared `outs`, or a\nsanctioned `glob()`. `//tests:bazel_file_coverage` enforces this."},"2732":{"id":"/project-conventions-825","page_id":"/project-conventions","tags":["conventions","contributing","safety","bazel","style"],"type":"text","url":"/project-conventions#writing-it-bazel-first","content":"**List files by name by default.** A wildcard is allowed only where the tree is\ngenerated (`docs/generated/**`, `config/grafana/dashboards/*.json`), tool-owned\n(`lib/db/migrations/**`, `**/*.png` goldens), copied wholesale by a framework\n(`app/**`, `components/**`, `lib/**`, `**/*.tsx`), or follows the documented\ndrop-in convention (`scripts/lib/*.sh`, `scripts/utilities/*.sh`). Each one is\npinned with its reason in `SANCTIONED_GLOBS` in `tests/bazel_file_coverage.py`;\nadding a wildcard without adding its justification fails the gate, and a\nsanction whose pattern has disappeared fails it too."},"2733":{"id":"/project-conventions-826","page_id":"/project-conventions","tags":["conventions","contributing","safety","bazel","style"],"type":"text","url":"/project-conventions#writing-it-bazel-first","content":"A `glob()` whose pattern has no wildcard is a plain file name wearing a\ndisguise: write the string."},"2734":{"id":"/project-conventions-827","page_id":"/project-conventions","tags":["conventions","contributing","safety","bazel","style"],"type":"text","url":"/project-conventions#writing-it-bazel-first","content":"Anything a target reads at runtime belongs in its `data` list. When you add a\nmanifest that `scripts/lib/*.sh` applies, add its filegroup to `//scripts:manage`."},"2735":{"id":"/project-conventions-828","page_id":"/project-conventions","tags":["conventions","contributing","safety","bazel","style"],"type":"text","url":"/project-conventions#writing-it-bazel-first","content":"New package: give it a `\"\"\"Package purpose: …\"\"\"` docstring and a public `:all`\naggregate, then list that aggregate in `//:everything`."},"2736":{"id":"/project-conventions-829","page_id":"/project-conventions","tags":["conventions","contributing","safety","bazel","style"],"type":"text","url":"/project-conventions#adding-a-check","content":"Follow the `doc_coverage` shape: `tests/<name>.py` with `_repo_root()` and\n`_tracked()`, a `main()` that prints `  - <path>: <reason>` to stderr and returns\n1, a three-line `tests/<name>.sh` wrapper, a `tests/test_<name>.py` unit suite run\nby `tests/<name>_unit.sh`, two `sh_test` targets in `tests/BUILD.bazel`, and the\nlabels added to `_TEST_FAST` in the root `BUILD.bazel`. Then add a row to the\ncoverage-gate table above and to tests/README.md."},"2737":{"id":"/project-conventions-830","page_id":"/project-conventions","tags":["conventions","contributing","safety","bazel","style"],"type":"text","url":"/project-conventions#adding-a-new-inference-workload","content":"Copy `k8s/workloads/kimi-test/` structure (job, service, kustomization, README, BUILD.bazel)"},"2738":{"id":"/project-conventions-831","page_id":"/project-conventions","tags":["conventions","contributing","safety","bazel","style"],"type":"text","url":"/project-conventions#adding-a-new-inference-workload","content":"Set conservative `resources.requests`/`limits`, `restartPolicy: OnFailure`, low `backoffLimit`"},"2739":{"id":"/project-conventions-832","page_id":"/project-conventions","tags":["conventions","contributing","safety","bazel","style"],"type":"text","url":"/project-conventions#adding-a-new-inference-workload","content":"Add NCCL env vars for multi-node workloads"},"2740":{"id":"/project-conventions-833","page_id":"/project-conventions","tags":["conventions","contributing","safety","bazel","style"],"type":"text","url":"/project-conventions#adding-a-new-inference-workload","content":"Register in `config/resource-policy.yaml` + `.json`"},"2741":{"id":"/project-conventions-834","page_id":"/project-conventions","tags":["conventions","contributing","safety","bazel","style"],"type":"text","url":"/project-conventions#adding-a-new-inference-workload","content":"Add `get_model_job` mapping and `start-<name>` in `lib/models.sh` / `manage.sh`"},"2742":{"id":"/projec