uced from structured comments inside the scripts."],[3447,"The switch block (host, read-only user, `port_map`) lives in `lab.yaml`; the password is\n`LAB_SWITCH_PASSWORD` in the operator's environment only. Qwen 3.5 397B NVFP4 is the\ncanonical TP=4 Job here. Cabling and port map: Choose topology."],[3441,"The switch fabric is a managed 4× 400G QSFP-DD device; each node sees **one** RoCE link:"],[4477,"The switch is a managed 4-port 400G QSFP-DD device with a 10GbE management port:"],[4481,"The switch's management IP (e.g. `10.0.0.2`) is declared in the `switch:` block; only a\n**read-only** API probe may use it. The switch password is read from the\n`LAB_SWITCH_PASSWORD` environment variable at runtime — never commit it."],[32,"The traditional Makefile and direct `ansible-playbook` / `bazelisk run //:manage --` invocations remain available for compatibility and for people who have not installed bazelisk."],[62,"The visual suite serves the export itself (`playwright.config.mjs` `webServer` runs\n`scripts/serve_static.mjs`), so nothing has to be started by hand. It captures the ten pages\nwhose rendering carries risk — index, getting-started, architecture, models-catalog,\ntroubleshooting, reboot-safety, dgx-spark-notes, monitoring-observability, dev-workspaces,\ngitea-ci-setup — at both desktop and mobile widths, waits for hydration plus the client-side\nMermaid SVGs, and drives every animation and transition to its end state before capturing so\nbaselines are reproducible."],[6254,"THEME\\_STORAGE\\_KEY"],[7156,"themeId"],[6251,"ThemeMode"],[6001,"ThemeProvider"],[6008,"ThemeSelector"],[447,"Then install the dashboard and docs-site dependencies with `bazelisk run //dashboard:install` and `bazelisk run //docs-site:install`."],[793,"Then reboot workers, then spark0. Jobs will **not** come back. Full sequence: Reboot safety · Patch and reboot."],[3984,"Theory"],[1608,"There is **no** official DeepSeek-V4.1 / V4.1-Pro checkpoint. Local DeepSeek on this lab is **V4.1-Fl